/-!
# Local generation by sections under `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a`, at all seven comparison functors

Descent, Lemma 05VG compares the properties of Modules on Sites, Definitions 03DE, 03DL and
03ER across the comparison functors `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a` of Descent, Proposition 03DX.  This file settles
the clause of Definition 03DL (3), **local generation by sections**, at every one of the seven
functors 05VG speaks about: the five big sites `(Sch/S)_τ` for
`τ ∈ {Zariski, étale, smooth, syntomic, fppf}` and the two small sites `S_Zar` and `S_étale`.

## The route

The source's hypothesis is that `𝓕` is quasi-coherent, and that hypothesis already decides both
sides of the clause: a quasi-coherent sheaf of modules on *any* site is locally generated by
sections, because quasi-coherent data supplies, on each member of a covering of the final
object, a presentation whose generators are generating sections.  That is the implication
Definition 03DL (6) ⟹ 03DL (3), proved here as
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_of_localGeneratorsData` together with
Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.QuasicoherentData.localGeneratorsData`.

So the equivalence is obtained by proving each side outright.  On the scheme side
`SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherent` is Mathlib's predicate and `𝓕`'s own quasi-coherent data is
`SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherent.nonempty_quasicoherentData`.  On the site side the quasi-coherent
data of `𝓕^a` is the covering argument of Stacks 03DV, proved at all five big sites as
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseQuasicoherentDataAssociatedModule` and at the two small sites
as `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.quasicoherentDataAssociatedModule` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.quasicoherentDataAssociatedModule`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_of_localGeneratorsData`:
  **Modules on Sites, Definition 03DL (6) ⟹ 03DL (3)** in the form actually needed — local
  generators data, in an arbitrary index universe, gives local generation by sections.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_baseAssociatedModule_iff`:
  **Descent, Lemma 05VG for Definition 03DL (3) at the big site `(Sch/S)_τ`, at every `τ`.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_associatedModule_iff`:
  **the same at the small site for `τ = étale`.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.isLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite_associatedModule_iff`:
  **the same at the small site for `τ = Zariski`.**

## Implementation notes

Each of the three equivalences carries exactly the source's hypothesis, quasi-coherence of `𝓕`,
and no other.  The index type of a family of generating sections is unconstrained in
`SheafOfModules.IsLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite`, and nothing below constrains it: the index
type of the generators produced is the index type of the generators of the presentation supplied
by the quasi-coherent data, whatever that is.

The equivalence is *not* obtained by transporting the condition along the comparison, and
nothing here supplies such a transport.  The missing statement is
`((AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.pullbackModules f).obj F).IsLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite`
from `F.IsLocallyGeneratedBySectionsOnSite`, the analogue for Definition 03DL (3) of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_iff_pullbackModules`, which is
Stacks 03DM for the bounded clause 03DL (4).  The bounded clause gets it from
`Stacks.Sheaves.LocalGeneration.generatingTupleSheaf`
(`StacksFrontier/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/ToposPullbackLocalGeneration.lean:480`), the sheaf
of locally spanning `r`-tuples, which is indexed by `Fin r` throughout — as are
`Stacks.Sheaves.LocalGeneration.combinationValue`
(`ibid.:337`) and `linearCombination` (`ibid.:377`), the two linear-combination operations the
whole chain is built on.  An unbounded index type makes a linear combination a *finitely
supported* family of coefficients, so that chain would have to be rebuilt over `Finsupp`; its
extension-of-scalars half, `Stacks.Sheaves.LocalGeneration.extendScalars_isLocallyGeneratedBy`
(`ibid.:1201`), is the only half whose argument is already index-agnostic, through
`generatingSections_leftAdjoint_restrictScalars` (`ibid.:1076`).

That route would prove more than 05VG asks of this clause — the clause without quasi-coherence —
and the three statements below do not need it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05VG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05VG)
